## Context

Author question, 2026-10-29: when is the global consistency and organization
of the docs audited? Survey (PR 1945, ticket 1333): every doc check is
incremental: per change (gaze doc seat, roar step 6, `tests/test_root_doc_paths.py`),
per day (lair STATE and ROADMAP facts, yawn docs freshness), per visit on
skills and rules changed since the last harness-doctor entry. Nothing looks at
the whole doc set. The global audits so far were author-led one-offs:
`conception/2026-09-24-rules-coherence-audit.md`, the 2026-10-19 root-doc
refresh (`memory/journal/2026/2026-10-19-docs-refresh-and-global-claude-retirement.md`).

Author decision: give the global audit a home in harness-doctor, not a new
doctor and not more guards.

## Intent

A harness-doctor visit whose input is the whole doc set: root docs (README,
INSTALL, AGENTS, CONTRIBUTING, ROADMAP, STATE, RTK), `rules/`, `conception/`
index, skill references. Questions: one home per fact; pointers, not
restatement; does each document still hold what its role says; overlap and
gaps between documents. Findings follow the doctor's floor (ticket, fix
inline, or drop).

Lair suggests the visit, never starts it: 30 days after the last docs visit
journal entry, or when a ROADMAP workstream closes. Suggestion only, as for
the other doctor offers.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Harness-doctor names the docs visit (complaint area or default input) by pointer, within the body budget after ticket 1334 (150-line cap, scripts/skill_text_lint.py)
- [ ] Lair suggests it on the two triggers, suggestion only
- [ ] One visit run on the current tree, its journal entry committed, findings handled by the floor
- [ ] No new guard or test pinning wording

## Plan (raid 94edd2)

Blocked-by 1334 holds: both edit skills/harness-doctor/SKILL.md, which has a 150-line
cap (`MAX_BODY_LINES`, scripts/skill_text_lint.py); 1334's menu row lands first.

Actions: (1) measure the SKILL.md headroom after 1334. (2) Name the docs visit by pointer
in SKILL.md, its input list and questions in a reference; journal slug
`-harness-doctor-docs-` so a docs visit is distinguishable from other visits. (3) Lair
suggestion step shaped like its existing suggestion steps, suggestion only: the 30-day
trigger reads the newest `*-harness-doctor-docs-*` entry date; the workstream trigger is
a reading of ROADMAP.md, judgment, no script. (4) Run the visit on a pinned commit,
commit the journal entry, findings by the floor. No new test pinning wording.
